[{:db/id "q-14319/selection/87461cebe4b3216a28ac7238f5a2547f52b6d01d84a8deb06a4225d4b771c191" :answer/id #uuid "e1974ae0-b2e1-56f8-bc06-da719dacb176" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14319/selection/cdde63ef388b1db418199f25fdcc08a2f04758364fb7753a89f05125d9b95c9c" :answer/id #uuid "b8d94ee0-0dc8-5284-8414-c6c540b932aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{{y}^{3}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14319/selection/03df5196009e09dc3d85e0eaec564df90e05a6f3b189eb51d76a6f9616946ecb" :answer/id #uuid "09e4268c-79a8-54aa-bf1c-aab521c18684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3xy+xy}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14319/selection/905bb50df679fbc14153d3d6a4f17a3278cc9e53765eb7c4c228c950f46c7a96" :answer/id #uuid "ccf0814b-0865-5a1a-a668-05f9e03eed36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14319/selection/c987e01ab3988c1090c58b45e211a8d328b560cec4a4d34b4507354cd4d9108f" :answer/id #uuid "fd40ea91-b19a-5d61-9f5e-778cf9724345" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}x-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14319/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c463f5e-1065-59e9-86e1-409018d6e4fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14319/selection/905bb50df679fbc14153d3d6a4f17a3278cc9e53765eb7c4c228c950f46c7a96" :answer-field/choices ["q-14319/selection/87461cebe4b3216a28ac7238f5a2547f52b6d01d84a8deb06a4225d4b771c191" "q-14319/selection/cdde63ef388b1db418199f25fdcc08a2f04758364fb7753a89f05125d9b95c9c" "q-14319/selection/03df5196009e09dc3d85e0eaec564df90e05a6f3b189eb51d76a6f9616946ecb" "q-14319/selection/905bb50df679fbc14153d3d6a4f17a3278cc9e53765eb7c4c228c950f46c7a96" "q-14319/selection/c987e01ab3988c1090c58b45e211a8d328b560cec4a4d34b4507354cd4d9108f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14319" :question/id #uuid "2c7b784c-55b7-51ac-a3da-61aa471e2821" :question/math-academy-id "q-14319" :question/problem "Which of the following is a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}.$\n\nWe see that both the numerator and denominator are homogeneous polynomials of degree $3.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $3-3=0.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)^{3}-3(tx)^{2}(ty)+(tx)(ty)^{2}}{(ty)^{3}+(tx)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}({x}^{3})-{t}^{3}(3{x}^{2}y)+{t}^{3}(x{y}^{2})}{{t}^{3}{y}^{3}+{t}^{3}{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})}{{t}^{3}({y}^{3}+{x}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-14319/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8c2a855-07a3-5855-9f6c-1a914953ac53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14319"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8369/selection/aa2714b7d3dec6193b14ee35d452a59cd94a6882454adb59a60dd84bcb2b094f" :answer/id #uuid "72f9d622-90d7-523a-a76b-14f44aee31b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{y-{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8369/selection/80515c47759e01fffdff039bbf6bad3c411e4447dc98ae0140749030d185b3ce" :answer/id #uuid "190f4372-c897-5083-a24e-307e2c834ca2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8369/selection/15901b89f31f4fa938a35662930fd6ae65d79308a89985b525593942d133a463" :answer/id #uuid "14ca282c-37e1-59ec-8fd7-c4cbe5347936" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8369/selection/3d4413e86f4150db897292b00eaede004b3601daaf453ec545f3bed3aa86b4fb" :answer/id #uuid "442138ad-837f-5e1c-bec0-3f41d04a9e51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8369/selection/6c94c42d1f90906af92b16efa8285624e42775ffe2c22ca3752a4c9c955cb8fd" :answer/id #uuid "d697354e-8a56-58da-96c2-3635505d969f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8369/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "242eec18-5d8e-59e6-aba1-35057e4c3f5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8369/selection/6c94c42d1f90906af92b16efa8285624e42775ffe2c22ca3752a4c9c955cb8fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-8369/selection/aa2714b7d3dec6193b14ee35d452a59cd94a6882454adb59a60dd84bcb2b094f" "q-8369/selection/80515c47759e01fffdff039bbf6bad3c411e4447dc98ae0140749030d185b3ce" "q-8369/selection/15901b89f31f4fa938a35662930fd6ae65d79308a89985b525593942d133a463" "q-8369/selection/3d4413e86f4150db897292b00eaede004b3601daaf453ec545f3bed3aa86b4fb" "q-8369/selection/6c94c42d1f90906af92b16efa8285624e42775ffe2c22ca3752a4c9c955cb8fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8369" :question/id #uuid "29260781-8760-5b93-aff1-74357dc9fb2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-8369" :question/problem "Which of the following is a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}.$\n\nWe see that both the numerator and denominator are homogeneous polynomials of degree $2.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $2-2=0.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(ty)^{2}-(tx)^{2}}{(ty)^{2}+(tx)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}{y}^{2}-{t}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{t}^{2}{y}^{2}+{t}^{2}{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})}{{t}^{2}({y}^{2}+{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8369/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8c2a855-07a3-5855-9f6c-1a914953ac53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90597/selection/cf7a69b962eede1e83dcf362a09ec5ca00056f5c76b11679212afd429410413d" :answer/id #uuid "5c1165d8-e0d1-5593-a01c-c4e5d4ab80ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90597/selection/695f47fc2f6231776d288fd67c348bc6c556927d566f3f6ef3818e7085cd1672" :answer/id #uuid "91c4cf49-08d9-5786-9604-ed9b592f0f25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90597/selection/fb66a4d7bc5d5bce2f0f1101b7d9d87715968ec409fc9f4b617e8c4610482aa0" :answer/id #uuid "0b792766-334a-510d-afb2-9df445a1504a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90597/selection/fd027e8dd77ef2e6888e1a75967e9b3bd181a583ec41329ac8370258b0d81743" :answer/id #uuid "f144672b-302e-5dab-b572-9c643d8e04fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{3}})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90597/selection/7b3aac85d64b4386e1aca3f6b94c924d988a7a5346f4a16ab17ad20f899b0a8e" :answer/id #uuid "18f8b35a-1ace-54e1-9d26-968183cdea42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90597/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2dba84e5-66b0-51da-b273-8ce153009b18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90597/selection/fb66a4d7bc5d5bce2f0f1101b7d9d87715968ec409fc9f4b617e8c4610482aa0" :answer-field/choices ["q-90597/selection/cf7a69b962eede1e83dcf362a09ec5ca00056f5c76b11679212afd429410413d" "q-90597/selection/695f47fc2f6231776d288fd67c348bc6c556927d566f3f6ef3818e7085cd1672" "q-90597/selection/fb66a4d7bc5d5bce2f0f1101b7d9d87715968ec409fc9f4b617e8c4610482aa0" "q-90597/selection/fd027e8dd77ef2e6888e1a75967e9b3bd181a583ec41329ac8370258b0d81743" "q-90597/selection/7b3aac85d64b4386e1aca3f6b94c924d988a7a5346f4a16ab17ad20f899b0a8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90597" :question/id #uuid "02b38e2b-182e-5e7d-8ad7-efb6ba37c64c" :question/math-academy-id "q-90597" :question/problem "Which of the following is NOT a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is NOT the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}.$\n\nWe see that it is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $2.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\,\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is not homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(ty)^{2}}{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is NOT homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90597/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8c2a855-07a3-5855-9f6c-1a914953ac53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8739"] :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$\n\nWe see that both the numerator and denominator are homogeneous polynomials of degree $2.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $2-2=0.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{2(tx)(ty)}{(tx)^{2}+(ty)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}\\cdot 2xy}{{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{{t}^{2}\\cdot 2xy}{{t}^{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8741"] :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is NOT the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=x.$\n\nWe see that it is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $1.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x\\,\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is not homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =tx=tf(x,y)\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is NOT homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-8747/selection/0ce347f39ef4bcbecfb916b81c9442e4dc61e0eef182193770d3ae044ec7d16a" :answer/id #uuid "b3c4bd59-d8a5-5d14-b03a-e27898e0a0cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}-v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8747/selection/4f9145894fec50f466ab35acc0acaa70f5435e9f7b5e530cfa4be9fc8bdeb4f4" :answer/id #uuid "291aecb2-71a8-5607-8db3-1a7b23ab4df0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}-3{v}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8747/selection/251569570557c9b507f56d7b0cdc61649e9a2aab677d7fdc152a69e99e6cabf6" :answer/id #uuid "c88b7aa5-224c-5264-b2ab-b293acc5894c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡v}+3}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8747/selection/aebc623af83548dbad02d0c62e1e8810edd516bcf3c6ae91aa11f0e05566c728" :answer/id #uuid "af8a1fc3-fc1b-5753-8ee0-b05e7ebba40b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8747/selection/8e5f5dde918157948b6e619181664f3c7fbf6ce9a93702fa8e000691fd8d0404" :answer/id #uuid "9ff96ecd-03cd-551a-9775-7ad4db15065d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡v}-5v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8747/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1eebb0b9-f7b4-5b1b-b702-2c54d53adfbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8747/selection/0ce347f39ef4bcbecfb916b81c9442e4dc61e0eef182193770d3ae044ec7d16a" :answer-field/choices ["q-8747/selection/0ce347f39ef4bcbecfb916b81c9442e4dc61e0eef182193770d3ae044ec7d16a" "q-8747/selection/4f9145894fec50f466ab35acc0acaa70f5435e9f7b5e530cfa4be9fc8bdeb4f4" "q-8747/selection/251569570557c9b507f56d7b0cdc61649e9a2aab677d7fdc152a69e99e6cabf6" "q-8747/selection/aebc623af83548dbad02d0c62e1e8810edd516bcf3c6ae91aa11f0e05566c728" "q-8747/selection/8e5f5dde918157948b6e619181664f3c7fbf6ce9a93702fa8e000691fd8d0404"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8747" :question/id #uuid "59df5070-dbd8-5482-bf07-a719f7cd3b66" :question/math-academy-id "q-8747" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{vx}{x})} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}-v \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}-v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8747/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8747"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14316/selection/08fae44cd84d868ec95d407e450bfcd8f22eb19e268c60264421fe72ee01fe37" :answer/id #uuid "1ff69b2f-8ab9-55fc-95ac-e06055ef4cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-v-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14316/selection/9308ac3c34324cb98285ac419d6ea711f0f12a1e9f50765e1a2dbf1044e3a7ca" :answer/id #uuid "08d5a410-9b73-5792-80be-c96b14a09b04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14316/selection/b9f2f7b41035e4310a7ea74c4c3c5be4c801b2792d25f4b05a3d3afff7e457ea" :answer/id #uuid "dc0ed936-8649-5ea2-b4a6-d868e8720314" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1+v+4{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14316/selection/607eab06fed26aa0392f85af8c2e12e0bb13f329e5f7e2fe67a59f7ada237464" :answer/id #uuid "4f6536c1-66ff-5a00-a09b-46708deaac9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-3v-4{v}^{2}}{1+{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14316/selection/c603976e19a70f49677471abc6cace683722b7e07b09e8badd6c5d3e4f76c4ce" :answer/id #uuid "5402799d-4127-507b-bcf5-4fc4e363902b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-3v-4{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14316/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a13ff3d7-c434-5801-8915-f8f36749bcd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14316/selection/9308ac3c34324cb98285ac419d6ea711f0f12a1e9f50765e1a2dbf1044e3a7ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-14316/selection/08fae44cd84d868ec95d407e450bfcd8f22eb19e268c60264421fe72ee01fe37" "q-14316/selection/9308ac3c34324cb98285ac419d6ea711f0f12a1e9f50765e1a2dbf1044e3a7ca" "q-14316/selection/b9f2f7b41035e4310a7ea74c4c3c5be4c801b2792d25f4b05a3d3afff7e457ea" "q-14316/selection/607eab06fed26aa0392f85af8c2e12e0bb13f329e5f7e2fe67a59f7ada237464" "q-14316/selection/c603976e19a70f49677471abc6cace683722b7e07b09e8badd6c5d3e4f76c4ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14316" :question/id #uuid "d4adf8ff-bd0d-5c23-b057-08c8deed164b" :question/math-academy-id "q-14316" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-x(vx)+(vx)^{2}}{(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(1-v+{v}^{2})}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-14316/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14316"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186088383 :question/answer-fields 17592186087228] {:db/id "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/7df65b5d634e47b9feb17e1ad1ad3c2dcb86d324655230d5a19c48d95c73bb06" :answer/id #uuid "f752bb46-e56c-54c2-b71f-905e661da16c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/d94246926d64828f0f6d535163f3664335c53190031e2105630270d680e3f682" :answer/id #uuid "e6c57563-fcbc-5ec9-a911-d06d5bf24720" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2v+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/b142f70db5ca0a348d1ed75e4023fcb534adbe90e9d194a70bdbe9b9b521a6b3" :answer/id #uuid "b8012b6a-0b93-5163-ac62-132c3f364316" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/2091ef9244c99ecf476660f0c3afe69b4f933e2d5a1b6fc68d031d0dc01c8303" :answer/id #uuid "ec586296-df27-5f73-bbd3-9db6ebbe9423" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{v+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/7256dff234443874950566086983a2376c7942be6a384928e72e89ac02282614" :answer/id #uuid "ac871b9d-852e-5be0-8ac3-f3091ce694da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a" :answer-field/id #uuid "891dcd85-6ba6-5872-a203-1e2e2038527b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/b142f70db5ca0a348d1ed75e4023fcb534adbe90e9d194a70bdbe9b9b521a6b3" :answer-field/choices ["q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/7df65b5d634e47b9feb17e1ad1ad3c2dcb86d324655230d5a19c48d95c73bb06" "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/d94246926d64828f0f6d535163f3664335c53190031e2105630270d680e3f682" "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/b142f70db5ca0a348d1ed75e4023fcb534adbe90e9d194a70bdbe9b9b521a6b3" "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/2091ef9244c99ecf476660f0c3afe69b4f933e2d5a1b6fc68d031d0dc01c8303" "q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a/7256dff234443874950566086983a2376c7942be6a384928e72e89ac02282614"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8745"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})+\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{vx})+\\frac{vx}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{1}{v}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8745/selection/ma-v1/10d7d107257915251504ce4cfe5999395a52580f81382e871b9eefb00d11398a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-14315"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+y{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3{v}^{3}{x}^{3}}{v{x}^{3}(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3{v}^{3}\\cancel{{x}^{3}}}{v\\cancel{{x}^{3}}(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}}{v+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}}{v+1}-\\frac{v(v+1)}{v+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}-{v}^{2}-v}{v+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2{v}^{2}-v}{v+1} \\\\ (\\frac{v+1}{2{v}^{2}-v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-14314/selection/e7c200884e80464355516b0e5230ed1faf773e2a2fbaff8fd70d40008dac8260" :answer/id #uuid "7d93d88a-9043-513a-96fc-1fbbfa5eecac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})+2{v}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14314/selection/b3e662b218368be2c7f7e8cc1c9c500fedf6f99ea54725d16efe720ef58a0bfb" :answer/id #uuid "449d2319-9d7f-5572-8c57-87de7c178807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}))\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14314/selection/858d28e3869674733617374848d46bfa942b9bb24d97636c513541a6d23ee0b7" :answer/id #uuid "98e21887-70b6-5d9f-a59a-65c42892d51a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})+v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14314/selection/d53a3ec3ee05c61f0e392c79681222309de8301835e4faaf80804efe31c5dd36" :answer/id #uuid "6e147765-48f3-501f-b446-ad145cc52a53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14314/selection/97c6c274f81f77382277b2d438b9ca2e8797d40626b24dd066f3b19daf63d3f5" :answer/id #uuid "ff0a5320-8873-5fc7-a010-a63c0b44d79c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14314/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c35e0ee-e673-5d29-81a2-1d81a15b0156" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14314/selection/97c6c274f81f77382277b2d438b9ca2e8797d40626b24dd066f3b19daf63d3f5" :answer-field/choices ["q-14314/selection/e7c200884e80464355516b0e5230ed1faf773e2a2fbaff8fd70d40008dac8260" "q-14314/selection/b3e662b218368be2c7f7e8cc1c9c500fedf6f99ea54725d16efe720ef58a0bfb" "q-14314/selection/858d28e3869674733617374848d46bfa942b9bb24d97636c513541a6d23ee0b7" "q-14314/selection/d53a3ec3ee05c61f0e392c79681222309de8301835e4faaf80804efe31c5dd36" "q-14314/selection/97c6c274f81f77382277b2d438b9ca2e8797d40626b24dd066f3b19daf63d3f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14314" :question/id #uuid "de0afd56-302d-5546-b6ff-08ceea918dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-14314" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})+\\frac{3y}{x}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})+\\frac{3y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{v}^{2}{x}^{2}})+\\frac{3vx}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+3v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v \\\\ (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-14314/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14314"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90692/selection/b0a444d0bc927f11bd9f73cf8c45579d3170e84eed637950e09701e3aabafb37" :answer/id #uuid "2e2c148a-1b6d-5d0c-acfa-edfb66c104c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C{x}^{2}+2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90692/selection/ddbe220cc55052feee01974415a7f64a35391827712c061a5c4b7f827a25e3fa" :answer/id #uuid "931b0fc2-e492-58c6-aac5-872c3b042560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C{x}^{3}+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90692/selection/d2fc1ecf3392b6ff953a2425fd3512740f6f016b9f7a8add5212baa072df4289" :answer/id #uuid "8d8123c8-0153-5fa2-a77c-450ed9e41027" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C{x}^{3}-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90692/selection/acaa0084ca385eaf7dbcce7d48bb3fdc24d0b43d2efbe1810d9b8874c3b97264" :answer/id #uuid "96b473c7-b5f9-59c4-8ce2-b869e961e208" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90692/selection/d548e6039c6ca27d46652f801d6bac1be1431189357f0190c4f8d27200df8e06" :answer/id #uuid "8d4a22ff-fc4e-5e92-918f-c3c611a82c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=C{x}^{2}-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90692/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "805137da-dc26-5238-b8a3-91d0a7a915d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90692/selection/d548e6039c6ca27d46652f801d6bac1be1431189357f0190c4f8d27200df8e06" :answer-field/choices ["q-90692/selection/b0a444d0bc927f11bd9f73cf8c45579d3170e84eed637950e09701e3aabafb37" "q-90692/selection/ddbe220cc55052feee01974415a7f64a35391827712c061a5c4b7f827a25e3fa" "q-90692/selection/d2fc1ecf3392b6ff953a2425fd3512740f6f016b9f7a8add5212baa072df4289" "q-90692/selection/acaa0084ca385eaf7dbcce7d48bb3fdc24d0b43d2efbe1810d9b8874c3b97264" "q-90692/selection/d548e6039c6ca27d46652f801d6bac1be1431189357f0190c4f8d27200df8e06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90692" :question/id #uuid "ba95a3f6-3e84-5b76-8295-96b17f255549" :question/math-academy-id "q-90692" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+2y}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+2y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{x+2(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{x(1+2v)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =1+2v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =1+v \\\\ \\frac{1}{1+v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{1+v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v+1| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v+1| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{{C}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v+1| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{{C}_{1}}|x|) \\\\ |v+1| & ={e}^{{C}_{1}}|x| \\\\ v+1 & =\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}}x \\\\ v+1 & =Cx \\\\ v & =Cx-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have let $C=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x} & =Cx-1 \\\\ y & =C{x}^{2}-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90692/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90692"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90691/selection/49346dc1337a3d8650b416ed465dc75e1855ff86f73c40c60e6b08c8c01e3329" :answer/id #uuid "3dd5f8e4-5c74-5671-9519-d27f02139942" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90691/selection/a859368010cb81a563fd2555e5e42be31c6215c91ceece5ac0c7af4d6fc22f54" :answer/id #uuid "9e41ad29-590b-572d-ae11-c3ee5b9b63e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90691/selection/91e709eaf00af96d2c7a9858653be932d60992bb327ee47cfb2fd7eab399a962" :answer/id #uuid "e0a2f70f-8de8-5842-851d-a0a6db439e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90691/selection/b0b94e6286e72ce119a7ffd9c059d5cb2adefb15aedc1497c9fc4c711c8b6348" :answer/id #uuid "af26cd02-707e-5f19-bcdd-10c5f7a95bb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90691/selection/364b34c9e2e926bdf9612e3c70b65cf8a5fb0875aa1e98e63f917f16015e2d8a" :answer/id #uuid "961066fa-4c79-5a20-b5ca-b8e9074b4f8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x{(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90691/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee04de02-8d8d-5d80-9526-285e6128e8d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90691/selection/49346dc1337a3d8650b416ed465dc75e1855ff86f73c40c60e6b08c8c01e3329" :answer-field/choices ["q-90691/selection/49346dc1337a3d8650b416ed465dc75e1855ff86f73c40c60e6b08c8c01e3329" "q-90691/selection/a859368010cb81a563fd2555e5e42be31c6215c91ceece5ac0c7af4d6fc22f54" "q-90691/selection/91e709eaf00af96d2c7a9858653be932d60992bb327ee47cfb2fd7eab399a962" "q-90691/selection/b0b94e6286e72ce119a7ffd9c059d5cb2adefb15aedc1497c9fc4c711c8b6348" "q-90691/selection/364b34c9e2e926bdf9612e3c70b65cf8a5fb0875aa1e98e63f917f16015e2d8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90691" :question/id #uuid "9c7628a4-6ce5-5421-9e03-8195e780eaca" :question/math-academy-id "q-90691" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{3})}{{v}^{2}{x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ {v}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {v}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+3{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have let $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{{x}^{3}} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C) \\\\ y & =x\\sqrt[3]{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14321/selection/9750fd0255595034f2e43f03b31d71af7987d02258f99c105b17cc0ae1ede183" :answer/id #uuid "bc633487-0bf1-5aa3-b454-99e596fa52f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14321/selection/2d8e2c1367d93a77906db341c04c900a6198cf776840085da9bb059b73cfb99e" :answer/id #uuid "83f2d7f8-3ad1-5422-8b19-31f60a1b04e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14321/selection/9796a3a1385529be026fae2ae53cd770b137c07dc1360ab12645d58267557017" :answer/id #uuid "b3e39a35-fedc-5e18-94c9-09f375e9c478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14321/selection/abe1202d852013bd02d78a868a258d154070b440fbed2a1c228837137e212079" :answer/id #uuid "4c862b7a-63f1-5bcc-a1c8-4288fd52a801" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=x(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14321/selection/934da978cf2dc1d56346b027f03d3609b2944f24d758b0e641feb6833b5e518c" :answer/id #uuid "bd39ad16-01f7-5d31-ab99-35997a1884f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14321/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "48afae7e-3aa4-57ac-a63d-e10bb01637bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14321/selection/9796a3a1385529be026fae2ae53cd770b137c07dc1360ab12645d58267557017" :answer-field/choices ["q-14321/selection/9750fd0255595034f2e43f03b31d71af7987d02258f99c105b17cc0ae1ede183" "q-14321/selection/2d8e2c1367d93a77906db341c04c900a6198cf776840085da9bb059b73cfb99e" "q-14321/selection/9796a3a1385529be026fae2ae53cd770b137c07dc1360ab12645d58267557017" "q-14321/selection/abe1202d852013bd02d78a868a258d154070b440fbed2a1c228837137e212079" "q-14321/selection/934da978cf2dc1d56346b027f03d3609b2944f24d758b0e641feb6833b5e518c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14321" :question/id #uuid "8b60ebca-2ed3-5d6e-85d9-d8b6f959696f" :question/math-academy-id "q-14321" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This is a homogeneous equation because it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y),\n$$\n\nand we notice that all terms in the numerator and denominator of $f(x,y)$ are of order $3$ (i.e., they are cubic).\n\nUsing the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{3}+x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)+{x}^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}({v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1)}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1-{v}^{3}-{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v+1}{v(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{v} \\\\ v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int v\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-14321/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8844"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{xy}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This is a homogeneous equation because it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y),\n$$\n\nand we notice that all terms in the numerator and denominator of $f(x,y)$ are of order $2$ (i.e., they are quadratic).\n\nUsing the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{xy} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{2}-{x}^{2}}{x(vx)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}-1)}{v{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{2}-1}{v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{2}-1-{v}^{2}}{v} \\\\ v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int v\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+C{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-90688/selection/aa608eaedacee9d3a776f1166ed29e1437681b1395cbc0d430eb9ed3a808ae4f" :answer/id #uuid "c0e3dccc-1dad-5a78-95e7-17990ca580cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{4}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90688/selection/af28e2b2301b9f28631bc74733d7a5b1ad9ec13d94c9793b3c8958c2475b2208" :answer/id #uuid "515c11cd-45c3-53e8-9a7c-83cae1d95144" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}=4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90688/selection/64f40cf45b3dc3ccae0b97f09e5c5cd3d81398b6b9c2c164e6f2b4f8b4963a3f" :answer/id #uuid "5100e614-3d32-5529-83fd-dfcfbfbd4f94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90688/selection/d87b78edc558823b5051244d1c69721eda23959d65d6b6848fb9e6a0df4505bb" :answer/id #uuid "cfefebce-4815-58ca-ba3d-31f95d8a4682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{C+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90688/selection/9210e7a107d681f1e641f2965b1989cf8e22d082f416f2cd30a2dbc8e73b6fcb" :answer/id #uuid "0097ea7d-1374-535a-bcbf-8a0e6d34897a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{C+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}=2{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90688/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aba66406-4955-50e7-a669-cc484689a76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90688/selection/64f40cf45b3dc3ccae0b97f09e5c5cd3d81398b6b9c2c164e6f2b4f8b4963a3f" :answer-field/choices ["q-90688/selection/aa608eaedacee9d3a776f1166ed29e1437681b1395cbc0d430eb9ed3a808ae4f" "q-90688/selection/af28e2b2301b9f28631bc74733d7a5b1ad9ec13d94c9793b3c8958c2475b2208" "q-90688/selection/64f40cf45b3dc3ccae0b97f09e5c5cd3d81398b6b9c2c164e6f2b4f8b4963a3f" "q-90688/selection/d87b78edc558823b5051244d1c69721eda23959d65d6b6848fb9e6a0df4505bb" "q-90688/selection/9210e7a107d681f1e641f2965b1989cf8e22d082f416f2cd30a2dbc8e73b6fcb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90688" :question/id #uuid "dce3c9c6-345d-5b0b-83e8-80c875dff755" :question/math-academy-id "q-90688" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}{x}^{3}}{({v}^{2}+1){x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (v+\\frac{1}{v})\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v| & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v| & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({v}^{2}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}) & =C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})} & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90688/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90688"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-2393"] :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{x}$\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{x^2}$\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{2x}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^2}\\right)}$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    f(x, y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero, meaning that it satisfies\n\n$$\nf(tx, ty) = f(x, y).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at the right-hand side function in each differential equation.\n\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{x}$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(ty)}{(tx)} \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{t\\cdot y}{t\\cdot x} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, equation I is a homogenous differential equation.\n\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{x^2}$ is *not* a homogeneous function of degree $0.$ Rather, it is a homogeneous function of degree $-1\\mathbin{:}$\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(ty)}{(tx)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{t\\cdot y}{{t}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & ={t}^{-1}f(x,y)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, equation II is *not* a homogenous differential equation.\n\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{2x}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^2}\\right)}$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{ty}{2(tx)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{(tx)^{2}}{(ty)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{t\\cdot y}{t\\cdot 2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{t}^{2}{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, equation III is a homogenous differential equation.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-2301"] :question/problem "Use the transformation $y = vx$  (where $v=v(x)$) to rewrite the given first-order homogeneous ODE \n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}    =   \\cos \\left( \\frac {y} {x} \\right)\n$$\n\nas a separable ODE in $v$ and $x.$" :question/worked-solution "With $y = vx$ (where $v = v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging that into the differential equation and separating variables, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(v) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(v)-v \\\\ (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(v)-v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-2302"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/12aec388c94c8c4d4f2099b98f5a489d110fa3ef0d58e7895d9a425e49f8eb77.png)" :question/worked-solution "We note that this equation is a homogeneous first-order differential equation because\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/c3215663fd1a332f750b8af4049404061e2b1c64726c81572d1a1e76816bb718.png)\n\nThe given equation is not separable, but we can transform it into a separable equation by carrying out the substitution\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/7c57d5a7c4003269ba9eacf6240394f508347989a9d75665c7070e31cbdad701.png)\n\nCarrying out the substitution and separating variables, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/8ad7a31876bc67fa69ff24ed41badcf6531ddf52b2d1847af4b0b75595ab5bcd.png)\n\nIntegrating both sides, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/7a6577d6ac4f3f1fc100a2767d77509fbe211f7d3e7bc7a2bba027080e7e6ccd.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/4247e7a16afb46979bc6ecfc9ae10dc6c92d0f5f1ff5e1b2a1f412ec86a48a83.png) (with ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/9e71f72815a80396d1186bfed1047662e1d507561c7160d1c2d89c2f23421c09.png)) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/012dd077bd0f68f82ae37fa50d493e97bd67ac5ff9f301e48ca29e91b1af16ab.png) \n\nFinally, substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/f74fcd854fc4be51cd8eed8f4d0649bcc7cf11089a7aa2a7e7edd8d306693f78.png) and simplifying, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/05eae130ba10a3386a1c8621ecc3e3d3ec0bb7af352fb4c928cf8bf2d88c21a3.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/8939a3ee49356a0cc8515cce98d84ecf10279dad9d2f76fac07660d0f99a0d7b.png) Therefore, the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/assets/185e5a72b055183d70fb6d9dbc0227190a8114b80b2dc4193d8f542d5c85c0d7.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
